# On-disk keys, one per host in git_unattended_signing_hosts
# (roles/git/defaults/main.yml). Per-host by design and never copied between
# machines, which is exactly why this list grows by one line per host rather than
# sharing a single entry. Adding a host to that list means appending its
# ~/.ssh/id_signing.pub here AND registering the same key on GitHub as a Signing
# Key -- the two are separate trust stores, and GitHub's badge says nothing about
# whether `git log --show-signature` can verify locally.

